  "invariants": [
    "Dispute, proceeding, forum, party role and judgment remain distinct identities.",
    "One dispute can link multiple forum-qualified proceedings.",
    "Transfer, severance, consolidation, appeal, recognition and enforcement never merge proceeding identities.",
    "Party identities and forum organizations remain externally mastered.",
    "Claims, counterclaims and defenses remain proceeding-owned assertions.",
    "Allegation, admission, finding and legal conclusion never merge.",
    "Appeal never erases prior decisions, findings or evidence rulings.",
    "Reversal and set-aside are append-only authority acts.",
    "Access restrictions survive until an authorized successor changes them.",
    "Claimed amount never becomes confirmed debt.",
    "Financial provision requires a separately authorized accounting act.",
    "Non-destructive closure preserves memberships, relations, filings, evidence rulings, judgments and successor links, and never cascades deletion or tombstones to referenced records.",
    "Service, effect, finality, enforcement and knowledge times remain distinct.",
    "Dispute identifiers are never recycled.",
    "A dispute relation links two retained dispute identities and never merges, replaces or retires either identity.",
    "Case number, title, party, forum, year, ECLI and file digest never identify a dispute or a proceeding, alone or in combination.",
    "Dispute membership records only the typed relation and its validity interval; no review, remedy or enforcement content is mastered on it.",
    "Setting a decision aside never withdraws access to that decision, its findings, its evidence rulings or its provenance.",
    "The statistical view forbids re-identification and never discloses a single dispute."
  ],
